  "thumbnailAlt": "Employee Performance Review form beside a photo of two women having a cheerful work conversation at an office table with a laptop",
  "content": {
    "intro": "An employee performance review form is a form that records a manager's ratings of an employee's core competencies, progress on goals, strengths, development areas and goals for the next period, so both sides have a clear, written record of the review. This template follows the usual annual review structure and ends with employee comments and a typed acknowledgment.",
    "audience": "People managers, HR business partners and small business owners running annual, mid-year or probation reviews.",
    "useCases": [
      "Annual performance reviews tied to raises or promotions",
      "Mid-year check-ins on goals set at the start of the year",
      "End-of-probation reviews for new hires",
      "Project-based reviews for contractors or rotating team members"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Use the PDF templates feature to generate a filled PDF of each review for the employee's personnel file.",
      "Let managers save progress and resume, since a thoughtful review is often written over more than one sitting.",
      "Edit responses after the review meeting to add the employee's comments; the edit history shows what changed and when."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should an employee performance review form include?",
        "answer": "Employee and reviewer details, the review period, ratings on core competencies (job knowledge, quality, productivity, communication, teamwork, initiative, reliability), results against last period's goals, strengths, areas to develop, goals for the next period, an overall rating and space for employee comments and acknowledgment."
      },
      {
        "question": "What rating scale works best for performance reviews?",
        "answer": "A five-point scale from 'Unsatisfactory' to 'Outstanding' is the most common because it is easy to explain. Define each level in writing so different managers rate the same way."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should employees write a self-review first?",
        "answer": "Many companies ask for one. You can copy this form, change the wording to the first person and send it to employees a week before the manager's review."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does the employee's acknowledgment mean they agree?",
        "answer": "No. It usually only confirms the employee has seen and discussed the review. Employees can record disagreement in the comments box."
      }
    ]
  },
